WEBVTT

00:00:00.940 --> 00:00:02.600
The first thing we're going to do is grab

00:00:02.600 --> 00:00:06.680
our tourniquet, prepare it so that we can go

00:00:06.680 --> 00:00:11.080
ahead and place it high and tight around the

00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:12.780
extremity that has the amputation.

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:16.500
We're going to go ahead and get the velcro

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:20.920
portion as tight as possible so that we won't

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:23.240
have to twist the windlass as many times to

00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:24.660
get the bright red bleeding to stop.

00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:30.480
As you twist the windlass, you'll ensure that all

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:33.200
bright red bleeding has stopped before you finish securing

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:38.720
it. I'll then go ahead and place the time

00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:39.880
in which I apply it.

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:47.740
Example being 14:29. You'll then grab your roll of

00:00:47.740 --> 00:00:56.180
tape, securing it around the tourniquet in order to

00:00:56.180 --> 00:00:59.980
prevent it from moving around during transportation.

00:01:07.640 --> 00:01:10.380
So if you would notice, I placed the tourniquet

00:01:10.380 --> 00:01:12.660
high and tight over the clothing.

00:01:22.060 --> 00:01:25.900
I'll then go ahead and place a T for

00:01:25.900 --> 00:01:33.560
time and our current time on top of the

00:01:33.560 --> 00:01:36.920
white tape in order to let the next echelon

00:01:36.920 --> 00:01:39.200
of care know what time we placed this.

00:01:39.760 --> 00:01:42.060
Now I'll go ahead and continue performing my patient

00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:42.320
assessment.
